    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "This is AgriPulse Open Mic. I'm your host, Jeff Nally. Our guest this week is California's 19th District U.S. Representative Zollopkrin. AgriPulse Open Mic, struck you by edge dairy farmer co-operative, the Voice of Milk. Learn more at voiceofmilk.com. AgriPulse Open Mic continues with Congresswoman Zollopkrin next. Open Bike is brought to you by Edge Dairy Cooperative, the voice of milk. Edge provides dairy farmers in the Midwest with a strong voice, the voice of milk, in Congress, with customers, and within their communities. Edge is a progressive organization that represents all dairy farmers equally, recognizing both their differences and similarities. Now the number 4 dairy cooperative in the country based on milk volume, edge is amplifying the voice of its farmers. Now more than ever, dairy farmers need to be heard. Learn more at voiceofmilk.com This is AgriPulse Open Mike. Legislation to address farm labor needs in the country was approved by the U.S. House of Representatives that faces an uncertain future in the U.S. Senate. California, 19th District Representative Zollofgrid admits the Farm Worker Modernization Act isn't an exhaustive immigration bill, but does offer U.S. agriculture a way to find the workers needed to get the job done. Loprin says the bill is a first step toward reform of U.S. immigration policy.",
