  {
    "episode_id": 72718,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72718.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Well, we did it by talking to each other and more importantly listening to each other. And it wasn't just the members of Congress, we brought stakeholders in the industry together. The United Farm Workers Union sat down with a whole host of agricultural employers, Western growers, Florida fruits and vegetables, and the list goes on and on. And these are their disagreements, and we identified what they were, and we sorted through them. We reached conclusion and we never gave up and it went on for months. I mean, we really started in last March and really by mid-October, we reached a bill that we thought was a pretty good bill. It's a compromise. I mean, if I had written it by myself, it would be different. I'm sure that's true or the Republican members, but it was something we all felt would be better than the status quo and would move us forward. That was a good model of working together and I hope we can do it again on other subjects.",
