    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think so. I mean, what the President sent over to us, we just couldn't support. And so, really what Speaker Pelosi did was appoint a task force headed by Richie Neal, who is the Chairman of the Ways and Means Committee, and a whole bunch, I wasn't on it, but a whole bunch of other members of Congress representing different parts of our caucus, different parts of the country. And we changed a whole bunch of the proposals. to the point where the head of the FLCIO says he thinks we should go for. The pharmaceutical industry is not very happy, which probably means we're on the right track. But I think it helps a lot for ag. It helps a lot. I come from Silicon Valley for technology. I think it has improvements. over environmental concerns. So, yeah, I think it's a step forward. I mean, it's, you know, it's not everything, but it's better than the status quo.",
